      "description": "Watch Houston Dynamo vs Austin FC highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. The Texas rivalry took center stage in MLS on July 26, 2026, as Houston Dynamo FC and Austin FC locked horns in a matchup defined by high energy and tactical shifts. A First-Half Blitz The match ignited early as the attacking unit found its rhythm almost immediately. In the 12th minute, Mateusz Bogusz opened the scoring, finishing clinically after being played through by Ezequiel Ponce . The early breakthrough set a confident tone, and the pressure on the opposition defense remained relentless throughout the opening exchanges. That pressure told again as the half progressed. In the 29th minute, Guilherme Augusto turned provider, setting up Mateusz Bogusz for his second goal of the night. The momentum was now fully with the home side, and just three minutes later, Guilherme Augusto went from creator to finisher. After receiving a pass from Agustin Bouzat in the 32nd minute, he struck gold to extend the lead to three, effectively stunning the visitors before the halftime whistle. Defensive Discipline and Closing Stages The second half saw a shift in tempo as the game became more physical and contested in the middle of the park. Discipline became a factor, with yellow cards issued to Ilie Sanchez , Felipe Andrade , Besard Sabovic , and Lucas Halter . The referee worked hard to manage the rising tensions as both teams fought for every inch of grass in a much tighter 45 minutes. As the clock ticked down, a flurry of substitutions altered the dynamic, with players like Duncan McGuire and Joseph Rosales introduced to provide fresh legs. Despite late attempts to alter the scoreline during the seven minutes of stoppage time, the defensive lines held firm. The clinical finishing displayed in the first half proved to be the difference, securing a vital victory in this heated regional contest."
